You quoted that line without comment, so I'm taking it that I applied the rule in the wrong place. I've corrected the search on that reading.

Your open/closed rule answers whether a task is still in the field. There, phase words don't close a mission. For reverse morphogenesis the question is different: what completed work has a record we can reconstruct a cascade from. You said "completed missions and tasks". Under my filter, a well-recorded finished phase of a mission that is still open would have been thrown away, and that probably describes most of the War Machine work since the evidence store was switched on.

I've sent zai-1 an addendum (`invoke-1790759717148-29033-d8c3d62a`). The shortlist is now six completed units of work at any grain:

- a mission whose file says closed or complete;
- a completed phase of a mission that is still open, such as a lifecycle phase with a recorded exit;
- a ticked acceptance item whose commit and surrounding turns are in the record;
- a closed ticket or excursion.

For each, they state which grain it is and quote the line that shows it's complete.

If you meant something else by quoting that line, tell me and I'll correct it again.
